<div class="container" id="content">
    <div class="row">
            <div class="col-md-9 order-md-last">
                <main>
                                            <div id="electricity_annual_technology_baseline_(atb)_data_download"></div><h1>Electricity Annual Technology Baseline Data Download</h1><p>Before downloading Annual Technology Baseline (ATB) data, read the <a href="./disclaimer">disclaimer agreement</a> and this guide to <a href="./technical_limitations">technical limitations</a>. All files are stored on the <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://data.openei.org">Open Energy Data Initiative</a> (OEDI).&nbsp;</p><p>Corrections made since the initial release of the 2025 Electricity ATB are listed on the <a href="./errata">errata page</a>.</p>
    <div id="2021_atb_data"></div><h2>2025 ATB Data</h2><h3><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://data.openei.org/files/8759/2025_v1_Workbook_08-27-2026.xlsx">Download the 2025 ATB Excel Workbook</a></h3><p>Each year, the National Laboratory of the Rockies (NLR) ATB data are presented in an Excel workbook that contains detailed cost and performance data (both current and projected) for renewable and conventional technologies. The workbook contains a spreadsheet with data and calculations for each technology.&nbsp;</p>
    <div id="download_the_2021_atb_summary_csv_files"></div><h3><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://data.openei.org/s3_viewer?bucket=oedi-data-lake&amp;prefix=ATB%2Felectricity%2F">Download the 2025 ATB Summary CSV Files</a></h3><p>These CSV files summarize in database-friendly form the capital expenditures, operating expenditures, and capacity factor, as well as the financial assumptions and the levelized cost of energy, for each technology. They are reformatted from the summary section of the spreadsheet, which documents the underlying calculations and data. The same data are also available in <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://data.openei.org/s3_viewer?bucket=oedi-data-lake&amp;prefix=ATB%2Felectricity%2Fparquet%2F&amp;limit=50">Apache Parquet format</a>.</p>
    <div id="download_all_2021_tableau_workbooks"></div><h3><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://data.openei.org/files/8759/2025_v1_Tableau_Workbooks_08-27-2026%20(1).zip">Download All 2025 Tableau Workbooks</a></h3><p>The charts on the ATB website were developed in a set of Tableau workbooks. These 19 workbooks are available as a single zip file. You can download a single workbook by following the instructions below to download a PowerPoint, but click on Tableau Workbook in the download menu.&nbsp;</p><h3>Instructions To Download Any Tableau Figure as a PowerPoint</h3><ol><li>Navigate to the Tableau visualization on the webpage.</li><li>Use the interactive filters to develop the view that you want.</li><li>Click the download button in the lower right-hand corner.</li><li>Select “PowerPoint.”</li><li>Select “This View.”</li><li>Click “Download.”</li><li>Select “view” or “save” the export, which comprises the current view and the set of active selection filters in a PowerPoint file.</li></ol>
    <div id="download_all_related_data"></div><h3><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://data.openei.org/submissions/8759">Download All Related Data</a></h3><p>View the entire OEDI entry for the 2025 ATB, including links to all of the above, previous versions of the data, parameter data with detailed capital expenditures (CAPEX) breakdowns, example scripts, and more.</p>
    <div id="atb-calc_repository"></div><h2>ATB-calc GitHub Repository</h2><p>Python files and Jupyter notebooks for processing the ATB data and calculating metrics are available <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://github.com/NatLabRockies/ATB-calc">on GitHub</a>. The ATB team held a webinar covering some example use cases for ATB-calc and answered questions. A <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=UE_YTdK1WxM">recording</a> is available.</p>
    <div id="past_atb_data"></div><h3>Past ATB Data</h3><p>For data from past years—and an accompanying summary and documentation—see the <a href="/archive">ATB archives.</a></p>


                </main>
